  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday night through next Monday)\nIssued at 1224 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nOver the next few days, the upper ridge gradually shifts west and\nstrengthens, becoming centered over AZ by late in the work week. \nAdditional isolated convection can't be ruled out Thurs night, but\nchances are primarily north of the forecast area. Meanwhile, a \npotent shortwave rounding the ridge will lead to a sfc low over \nthe Midwest pushing a front southward, with guidance suggesting \nthis front reaches our CWA sometime on Fri. This front will offer \nat least a low chance (20%) of storms Fri PM, followed by a 'cool \ndown' over the weekend as highs fall into the mid/upper 90s. Prior\nto this front's arrival, high temps remain in the 100-105 range \noff the Caprock. Easterly upslope flow over the weekend will keep\nadditional low precip chances (15-20%) in the forecast Sat, \nprimarily for areas on the Caprock. Forecast soundings depict a \ndeep, well-mixed boundary layer, so any storms that do form will \nbe capable of sporadic gusty/damaging winds. Looking ahead, \nguidance suggests the ridge shifts back east, once again becoming \ncentered over eastern NM/western TX, in a similar position to \nwhere it is currently. This suggests a slight warming trend and \nminimal precip chances into early next week.",
